		(uuid "2dd56352-3e72-4190-b176-52b5c758f389")
	)
	(text "Two differential I2C links, one per sense node, plus the cable\ninterface carrying CNVR and the three phase bits.\n\nCONSTRAINTS\n\n1. I2C was not designed to cross a cable. The PCA9615 turns each\n   single ended open drain bus into a differential pair that\n   survives the cable, then turns it back at the far end.\n\n2. Channel A and channel B are two copies of one circuit drawn on\n   one page. They must never share a net. A uses I2C1 on PB6 and\n   PB7, B uses I2C3 on PA8 and PB4. Two separate peripherals, so a\n   read stall on one bus cannot block the other. One shared bus\n   would sit at 104 percent utilization and fail outright.\n\n3. V_DD(A) and V_DD(B) are both 3.3 V, not 5 V, even though the\n   datasheet prefers 5 V on the line side. The cable carries only\n   3.3 V, so the remote buffer can only run its line side at 3.3 V,\n   and the idle bias at both ends has to reference the same rail.\n\n4. The 100 ohm termination goes across each pair. The two bias\n   resistors go to the rails, one up to 3.3 V and one down to\n   ground, per pair. This board holds one end of the line. The far\n   end lives on the remote sense board.\n\n5. The bias and termination values here are provisional. They bind\n   on the impedance controlled layout, not on paper.\n\n6. On each cable facing line, the series resistor sits at the\n   connector and the pull up sits behind it, so a transient meets\n   the resistor first.\n\n7. EN is tied to 3.3 V. The part has an internal pull up and would\n   float high on its own, but a floating enable on a board that\n   lives for years is a liability and a wire costs nothing.\n\n8. The local I2C pull ups are 2.2k. The bus on this side sees only\n   the STM32 pin and the buffer, roughly 40 pF. The remote INA226\n   sits behind the buffer and adds no capacitance here.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n两条差分 I2C 链路，每个采样节点一条，外加承载 CNVR 和三位相位码的\n线缆接口。\n\n约束\n\n1. I2C 本来就不是为跨线缆设计的。PCA9615 把每条单端开漏总线转成能扛\n   过线缆的差分对，到对端再转回来。\n\n2. 通道 A 和通道 B 是同一套电路在同一页上画了两份。它们之间绝不能共\n   用任何网络。A 用 PB6 和 PB7 上的 I2C1，B 用 PA8 和 PB4 上的\n   I2C3。两个独立外设，这样一条总线读卡住不会拖住另一条。共用一条总\n   线的占用率会达到 104%，直接失败。\n\n3. V_DD(A) 和 V_DD(B) 都是 3.3 V，不是 5 V，尽管数据手册更倾向线路\n   侧用 5 V。线缆上只有 3.3 V，远端的 buffer 线路侧只能跑 3.3 V，\n   而两端的空闲偏置必须参考同一条电源轨。\n\n4. 100 欧端接电阻横跨在每一对差分线上。两个偏置电阻接到电源轨，每对\n   一个上拉到 3.3 V、一个下拉到地。本板持有传输线的一端，另一端在远\n   端采样板上。\n\n5. 这里的偏置和端接数值都是暂定的。它们要在阻抗受控的 PCB 布线阶段\n   才最终确定，不是在纸面上定。\n\n6. 每条面向线缆的信号线上，串联电阻放在接口一侧，上拉放在它后面，这\n   样瞬态先遇到电阻。\n\n7. EN 接到 3.3 V。这颗芯片内部有上拉，本来悬空也会是高电平，但在一\n   块要用很多年的板子上让使能脚悬空是隐患，而多接一根线不花任何成本。\n\n8. 本地 I2C 上拉是 2.2k。这一侧的总线只看到 STM32 的引脚和 buffer，\n   大约 40 pF。远端的 INA226 在 buffer 后面，不会给这一侧增加电容。"
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 303.53 133.604 0)
